nesFile (line 24):**\nSessionInfo is wrapped in `Option` because not all `.lines.json` files have a session (e.g. legacy files, or before any AI registers). The `skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\"` attribute means the `session` key is entirely absent from JSON when there is no session, rather than being `null`.",
